# Data Modeling & Schemas

## Placement

- Request/response DTOs: [apps/backend/src/infra/schemas/](mdc:apps/backend/src/infra/schemas)
- Database models (if any) should live in infra/db-related modules, not with DTOs.
- Close to repositories/services when specific to one domain.

## Conventions

- Name DTOs with clear intent (e.g., `FileEntryCreate`, `FileEntryRead`).
- Separate request vs response models.
- Keep external API DTOs stable; prefer additive changes and version when breaking (see [21-backend-api-contracts.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/21-backend-api-contracts.mdc)).
- Use explicit field types and defaults; avoid `Any`.
- Document optional fields with defaults and comments.

## Validation & serialization

- Validate inputs at API boundary; sanitize/normalize where necessary.
- Use `model_dump()`/`model_validate()` (pydantic v2) to convert.
- Keep response payloads minimal and privacy-aware.

## Compatibility

- Add new fields as optional for non-breaking changes.
- For breaking changes, version APIs and DTOs (e.g., `v2`).
- Coordinate schema changes with database migrations (see [23-db-migrations.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/23-db-migrations.mdc)).
